# rule.always.archive-the-wishers-words-verbatim

when the wisher says a word that **changes the work**, catch it verbatim before you distill it.

```
$route/.seeds/inventory.of=seeds._.md                # the SUMMARY
$route/.seeds/inventory.of=seeds.case=S$n-$slug.md   # one ENTRY per utterance (.said · .settled · .landed)
```

both owed, every time.

| when the wisher… | then |
|---|---|
| settles a question, coins a word, specifies a contract (path, flag, format) | archive it |
| corrects you, or asks a question whose answer changes the work | archive it |
| — or you are about to write *"the wisher asked for…"* | that needs a source: archive first |

- `.said` is verbatim in SUBSTANCE: repair typos, profanity (cut or `[placeholder]`), mangled paths; never word choice, order, or mid-thought corrections. test: would the speaker say *"that is what I typed, spelled right"*? else it is a rewrite, and belongs in `.settled`
- a seed is the seed of a CONCEPT: strip route, tools, errors; what stands is the seed. the environment (switch state, a broken tool) is not a seed

blocker: an utterance that changed the work with no seed · `"the wisher asked for X"` with no source · a `.said` whose sense was edited, or that ships a typo or profanity · entries with no summary · a bare-ordinal `case=` · a body that narrates the round · a `.landed` row that carries a reason.
